.TH NTPDATE 1 "2026-11-02" "Wunix" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ntpdate \- set the date and time via NTP
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBntpdate\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]... [\fISERVER\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBntpdate\fR sets the local date and time by polling Network Time Protocol (NTP) servers.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-q\fR
Query only \- do not set clock.
.TP
\fB\-b\fR
Force stepping time.
.TP
\fB\-u\fR
Use unprivileged port.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR
Silent mode.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Verbose output.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help and exit.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBtimedatectl\fR(1), \fBdate\fR(1), \fBtimesyncd\fR(8)
